Final Concept (Exam Summary)
Application configuration in Kubernetes is externalized using:
1️⃣ ConfigMaps
•	Store non-sensitive configuration
•	Used for environment variables or config files
2️⃣ Secrets
•	Store sensitive information
•	Base64 encoded
•	Used for passwords, tokens, certificates
Both can be consumed by pods using:
•	Environment variables
•	Volume mounts
Commands used:
kubectl create configmap
oc create cm
oc create secret
oc set env
oc set volume
oc extract
oc set data

